    "done_when": "At the committed head: (1) In cached_only mode, a candidate whose serving observation is absent from the probe cache, or older than its shelf life, has availability unknown and is offered to Jev with that state. Only a fresh observation reading refused or unavailable excludes it. A test covers absent, expired and fresh-refused, and fails at the base revision in a recorded log. (2) A backend declaring an endpoints_document (clive does) takes its availability from that document's serving verdict, through the same reader reckon flight uses for its serving column, so clive reads served when the document lists its configured model. A test with a fixture endpoints document shows this. (3) A live in-process cached_only pick for an exact documentation node, run from the main checkout's environment with this worktree on PYTHONPATH, offers clive (not excluded), and is quoted with its excluded list in docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/picker-cached-availability.html. (4) The gate is every tests/test_picker*.py file plus every test file under tests/ that imports reckon/crew/picker/snapshot.py (found by grep), run at base and head, with both failure-id sets listed and zero added.",
